PATCH 219: reconstruct FUN_0000_7bcf (a display-object per-type INIT method dispatched by d755's
near-vector, patch 169) -- the same DGROUP-near-offset base-loss class as the c296 roster family
(215/216/217/218).  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x7bcf-0x7c08.

Reached after patch 169's d755 dispatch was fixed to THREAD di (the object near-offset) into the called
per-type method (the asm keeps DI live across `call [si-0x1998]`; 169 previously called it with `()` so
7bcf got garbage 0xbf -> SIGSEGV).  With di threaded, 7bcf runs on the real object slot.  Ghidra treated
di as a HOST pointer (`*(param_1+0x1a)=...`) -> SIGSEGV; DS=DGROUP=0x1c00, every [di+N] is a DS-relative
byte/word field.  Reconstructed with the explicit g_mem+0x1c000 base + the asm byte/word widths (the
0x6dae==2 branch + the seg-0x2c7f template copy to DGROUP:di+0xbf via 1e27's near-offset dst).

Cascade-only => BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows (reached ONLY via the FIST_CASCADE mission
display-setup walk d755).  Default boot rc=0, mainmenu unchanged.  Sources pristine; fist.c via build/.
